---
import FeatureLayout from "@/layouts/FeatureLayout.astro";
---
<FeatureLayout
  title="PgDesigner CLI for CI/CD"
  description="Single binary CLI for PostgreSQL schema management: generate DDL, diff schemas, lint with 69 rules, generate test data, merge and import schemas. Zero dependencies."
  subtitle="Single binary, zero dependencies. Lint, diff, generate, and seed — all from your terminal or CI pipeline."
>

<h2>Seven commands, one binary</h2>

<pre><code>pgdesigner schema.pgd                           # open in browser UI
pgdesigner generate -o schema.sql schema.pgd    # DDL to file
pgdesigner diff old.pgd new.pgd                 # ALTER SQL to stdout
pgdesigner lint -f json schema.pgd              # lint with JSON output
pgdesigner testdata -seed 42 schema.pgd         # reproducible test data
pgdesigner convert -o project.pgd schema.pdd    # import from other formats
pgdesigner merge -o all.pgd core.pgd billing.pgd  # merge schemas into one
pgdesigner version                              # print version</code></pre>

<p>Every command accepts <code>.pgd</code>, <code>.pdd</code>, <code>.dbs</code>, <code>.dm2</code>, <code>.sql</code>, or a PostgreSQL connection string as input.</p>

<h2>Plug into your CI pipeline</h2>

<div class="not-prose space-y-4 mt-6 mb-8">
  <div class="rounded-lg bg-surface-alt border border-border-default p-4">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-accent-text mb-2">Lint on every PR</p>
<pre class="text-sm"><code>- name: Validate schema
  run: pgdesigner lint -s error schema.pgd</code></pre>
    <p class="text-xs text-muted mt-2">Exit code 1 if errors found → blocks the merge.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="rounded-lg bg-surface-alt border border-border-default p-4">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-accent-text mb-2">Generate migration on schema change</p>
<pre class="text-sm"><code>- name: Generate migration
  run: |
    git show origin/main:schema.pgd &gt; /tmp/old.pgd
    pgdesigner diff /tmp/old.pgd schema.pgd | tee migration.sql</code></pre>
    <p class="text-xs text-muted mt-2">Exit code is 0 with or without changes. With <code>-o</code>, the file is not written when there are no changes.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="rounded-lg bg-surface-alt border border-border-default p-4">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-accent-text mb-2">Seed test database</p>
<pre class="text-sm"><code>- name: Seed test data
  run: |
    pgdesigner generate schema.pgd | psql $DATABASE_URL
    pgdesigner testdata -seed 42 -rows 100 schema.pgd | psql $DATABASE_URL</code></pre>
  </div>
</div>

<h2>Command reference</h2>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Command</th><th>Flags</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>generate</code></td><td><code>-o</code></td><td>Full DDL to stdout or file</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>diff</code></td><td><code>-f sql|json</code>, <code>-o</code></td><td>Compare two schemas → ALTER SQL or JSON</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>lint</code></td><td><code>-f text|json</code>, <code>-s</code>, <code>-fix</code></td><td>Validate schema, auto-fix issues</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>testdata</code></td><td><code>-seed</code>, <code>-rows</code>, <code>-tables</code>, <code>-o</code></td><td>Generate realistic INSERT statements</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>convert</code></td><td><code>-o</code>, <code>-schema</code>, <code>-full</code></td><td>Import from .pdd/.dbs/.dm2/.sql/DSN</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>merge</code></td><td><code>-o</code>, <code>-layout both|base|overlay</code>, <code>-name</code></td><td>Merge several schemas into one .pgd; later files win on conflicts</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>Exit codes</h2>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr><th style="text-align:center">Code</th><th>Meaning</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td style="text-align:center"><code>0</code></td><td>Success, including a diff with changes</td></tr>
    <tr><td style="text-align:center"><code>1</code></td><td>Lint errors found, missing arguments, file not found or parse error</td></tr>
    <tr><td style="text-align:center"><code>2</code></td><td>Unknown flag</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>Visual editor flags</h2>

<p>Without a command, <code>pgdesigner</code> starts a local server and opens the editor in your browser:</p>

<pre><code>pgdesigner schema.pgd              # open a model
pgdesigner postgres://localhost/app # reverse-engineer a live database
pgdesigner -app schema.pgd         # Chrome/Chromium app window, no address bar
pgdesigner -port 8080 schema.pgd   # fixed port instead of a random one
pgdesigner -read-only schema.pgd   # disable every write operation</code></pre>

<p><code>-read-only</code> is how the public <a href="https://demo.pgdesigner.io">demo</a> runs. For a live database, <code>-schema</code> and <code>-full</code> work the same as in <code>convert</code>.</p>

<h2>Cross-platform, zero dependencies</h2>

<p>Single statically-linked binary. No runtime dependencies — no Go, no Node, no Python. Works on:</p>

<ul>
  <li><strong>macOS</strong> — amd64 + arm64, signed and notarized</li>
  <li><strong>Linux</strong> — amd64 + arm64</li>
  <li><strong>Windows</strong> — amd64 + arm64</li>
</ul>

<pre><code>curl -L https://github.com/vmkteam/pgdesigner/releases/latest/download/pgdesigner-linux-amd64.tar.gz | tar xz
./pgdesigner lint schema.pgd</code></pre>

<div class="not-prose mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-border-default">
  <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-heading mb-3">Related</p>
  <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
    <a href="/docs/cli" class="text-sm text-accent-text hover:underline">CLI Reference →</a>
    <a href="/features/diff" class="text-sm text-accent-text hover:underline">Diff & ALTER →</a>
    <a href="/features/lint" class="text-sm text-accent-text hover:underline">Schema Linter →</a>
  </div>
</div>
</FeatureLayout>
